  "live_records": {
    "q-152384": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152384",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{\\sqrt{32{z}^{5}}}{\\sqrt{8{z}^{3}}}$ given that $z>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we bring the quotient under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{32{z}^{5}}}{\\sqrt{8{z}^{3}}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{32{z}^{5}}{8{z}^{3}}}=\\sqrt{4{z}^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the expression inside the radical is a perfect square. So, we can continue simplifying by writing the expression as this perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{z}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}{z}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(2z)}^{2}} & = \\\\ |2z| & = \\\\ |2|\\cdot |z| & = \\\\ 2\\cdot |z| & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we are told that $z>0,$ so we have $|z|=z.$ Therefore, the final answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |z| & = \\\\ 2\\cdot z & = \\\\ 2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
